  "rules": [
    "Model forecasts exhibit a strong upward bias during periods of rising price momentum (e.g., May 10-13), consistently underestimating the immediate peak and overestimating subsequent volatility.",
    "When sentiment history shows a spike to +0.50, the model fails to capture the full magnitude of the price surge, resulting in an initial forecast that is significantly lower than the true outcome (e.g., Example 1 Day 2: Forecast 53.04 vs True 55.32).",
    "The model displays a 'mean reversion lag' error; it predicts a smooth continuation after a spike, whereas the true market exhibits sharp mean-reverting corrections immediately following the peak.",
    "Forecasts are overly sensitive to recent price history but ignore sentiment-driven volatility expansion, leading to underestimated standard deviations in high-sentiment regimes.",
    "In the first 5-7 days of the forecast horizon, the model systematically underestimates the true price by approximately 2-4 EUR during strong uptrends."
  ]
}
